1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,945
Watts and watt-hours. Power, energy, and
your daily budget.

2
00:00:05,665 --> 00:00:08,865
Watts are power: how fast energy flows,
right now.

3
00:00:09,045 --> 00:00:12,158
Watt-hours are energy: power, times how
long it flows.

4
00:00:12,338 --> 00:00:15,125
Like litres per second, and the litres in
a bucket.

5
00:00:15,845 --> 00:00:23,744
Our stream from episode one makes 245
watts, day and night. Times 24 hours:

6
00:00:23,744 --> 00:00:25,534
5,880 watt-hours.

7
00:00:25,714 --> 00:00:30,281
A 400 watt solar panel, in full sun for 3
hours, makes 1,200.

8
00:00:30,461 --> 00:00:33,808
More watts, but about a fifth of the
watt-hours.

9
00:00:33,808 --> 00:00:36,458
A UK December day averages nearer 300.

10
00:00:38,578 --> 00:00:41,893
List each load: its watts, times its hours
a day.

11
00:00:42,073 --> 00:00:47,887
A Starlink dish averages up to 100 watts,
all day. 2,400 watt-hours.

12
00:00:48,067 --> 00:00:52,346
A laptop uses 50 watts, for 4 hours. 200.

13
00:00:52,526 --> 00:00:58,405
Four 10 watt LED lights, for 5 hours:
another 200. Phone charging: about 20.

14
00:00:58,585 --> 00:01:04,606
Total: about 2,820 watt-hours. Under half
of what the stream makes.

15
00:01:06,526 --> 00:01:10,183
Where do the other three thousand go? The
stream never stops.

16
00:01:10,363 --> 00:01:13,915
A controller sends the spare to a dump
load: a heater for air or water.

17
00:01:15,235 --> 00:01:18,474
The one rule: a hydro generator never runs
without a load.

18
00:01:18,654 --> 00:01:22,049
Lose the load, and it overspeeds, and the
voltage spikes.

19
00:01:22,049 --> 00:01:27,052
So the dump load stays connected, big
enough to take everything the generator
makes.

20
00:01:27,232 --> 00:01:29,669
Shut the water off before you touch the
wiring,

21
00:01:29,669 --> 00:01:31,847
and have a qualified electrician check it.

22
00:01:33,567 --> 00:01:36,971
Remember: watts, times hours, gives
watt-hours.

23
00:01:37,151 --> 00:01:44,068
245 watts, all day, is nearly 6
kilowatt-hours. Keep your loads under what
you make,

24
00:01:44,068 --> 00:01:48,515
and, without a battery, under 245 watts at
any moment.

25
00:01:49,235 --> 00:01:52,387
Next: volts, amps and ohms, in one minute.
